  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Serbian Commissariat for Refugees and Migration (Commissariat) to Manage Mixed Migration at the National and Local Level - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than 1.5 million migrants have passed through Serbia since 2015. Even after the closure of the Western Balkan Route in March 2016, Serbia continued to face a high number of migrants. The main goal of the project is to further strengthen the migration management system in Serbia with a focus on strengthening the capacities of the Commissariat for Refugees and Migration (SCRM) in managing reception/accommodation facilities, identification, and referral of migrants in vulnerable situations, as well as counselling, and collection of reception data.</narrative>
  </description>
